---
title: ONI Merge base64
tags: tools
heading: "Merge Base64"
redirectFrom: /oni/mergeb64/
summary: >-
    Merges several Base64 strings into one, taking the most common character at each position.
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>For several copies of the same Base64, each with a few mistakes: where they disagree, the character most of them have wins, and a tie goes to the earliest string. Put each copy in its own box, and add more boxes as you need them, up to 10. Empty boxes are skipped.</p>
    <p>When the copies are different lengths, only those long enough count at each position, so the result is as long as the longest. The status line says how many positions they disagreed at.</p>
    <p>In the browser console: <code class="tool-example">convrtr.{{ filename }}(...strings)</code> gives the merged string, and <code class="tool-example">convrtr.compareBase64(...strings)</code> also counts the disagreements.</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Merge Base64", inputList = { label: "String", min: 2, max: 10, add: "Add a string", placeholder: "Example: SGVsbG8gV29ybGQh" }, actions = [{ id: filename + "Run", label: "Merge" }]) %}{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
